  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "AutoMapperLite 4.0.2 — current official release; all prior versions are deprecated.\n\n\t\t\t• Fixed: updated test tooling (xunit.v3, Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk 18.9.0) hard-required\n\t\t\t  net8.0+ and a Microsoft Testing Platform v2 change dropped dotnet test's legacy\n\t\t\t  VSTest bridge on the .NET 10 SDK — the test project now targets net8.0-net10.0 (the\n\t\t\t  library itself is unaffected and still targets net6.0-net10.0) and a repo-root\n\t\t\t  global.json opts dotnet test into native MTP mode\n\t\t\t• Fixed: Activator.CreateInstance failures (e.g. mapping to a positional record with\n\t\t\t  no parameterless constructor) now throw a clear InvalidOperationException naming\n\t\t\t  the type, instead of a bare MissingMethodException\n\t\t\t• Added real, measured BenchmarkDotNet comparisons against manual mapping, AutoMapper\n\t\t\t  16.2.0, and Mapster 10.0.12 — published in docs/performance.html; AutoMapperLite is\n\t\t\t  not the fastest of the four, and the docs/package description no longer claim\n\t\t\t  otherwise\n\t\t\t• Verified and documented several previously-untested behaviors: null source\n\t\t\t  properties are skipped (not assigned), auto-map requires an exact type match\n\t\t\t  (different enum types / numeric widening are not converted), and records with a\n\t\t\t  parameterless constructor + init-only properties map correctly\n\t\t\t• No public API breaking changes since 3.0.3",
